 "title": "The logistic map's fixed point",
 "caption": "A fixed point of x_{n+1} = rx_n(1 − x_n) is where the parabola meets the line y = x. For r = 2.5, x* = 1 − 1/r = 0.6. The slope there is f′(x*) = 2 − r = -0.5; since |f′| < 1 iterates spiral in and it is stable. For r = 3.2 the slope is −1.2 and a 2-cycle takes over.",
